Z||000005||Black88GT||11-26-2000||11:45 PM||||You asked for it.  That looks horrible.<BR>It looks like a red anvil dropped onto your Fiero or something.  I would think a ricer wing would look better.  Its almost like a hook that a crane could lift up your car with, or a missile launcher out of a James Bond flick.  Take that thing off and your car and it would look nice.  The Indy scoop looked OK but the imitation ones on the market aren't functional so there just dumb too.<P><BR>OK I'm done.<P>Its your scoop and if you like it who cares what anyone else thinks.  I will give you one thing, I have never seen it on any other Fiero so you have the originality award from me.<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000006||Seanh||11-26-2000||11:52 PM||||I like it, but I agree it should be tad lower. I would never have a scoop like that on my car because of the rear view resriction of it. Is it functional? By functional what do you guys mean, like just to cool the engine, or Ram-Air induction? Also, Oreif included, do you have any trouble opening your rear decklid?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||11-27-2000||12:05 AM||||Hugh,<BR>If it's needed, cool. <BR>Otherwise, I prefer something a little more low key, like the Mustang scoop. <BR>Definitely kicks the whole "sleeper" concept right in the head. <BR>I'll bet the engine likes all the cool air that it can gulp on the highway. <P>Raydar<BR>  ||||reg||1
