Z||000026||hugh||11-27-2000||09:05 PM||||First,I have to admit I didn't build this car.If I had,I think I would have done the same thing.The scoop does block the rear window a good bit,but that is what side mirrors are for.It can't be made lower without some major work on how it contacts the hood.It is functional and necessary as the pictures on this post show.I have a Lingenfelter Superram fuel injection system to put on when I get time(if I ever do).Then I might remove it just so the car doesn't stand out so much(but I doubt it).The car has the original radiator and never got over about 160 degrees the few times I drove it this summer,I have to believe the scoop helped.I would like to put it in a show,but it has been my experience with my 2 engine 70 Chevelle that if you don't belong to the sponser club you don't win.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://users.snip.net/~hlemma/fierotropen.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.snip.net/~hlemma/fierotropen3.jpg">   Some of your comments were a little rough,but's that's ok.I appreciate honesty.<p>[This message has been edited by hugh (edited 11-27-2000).]||||reg||1
